WEBVTT

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:03.389 line:94%,end align:center
ALBUM — Asset Localization By Unified Matching

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:06.790 line:94%,end align:center
ALBUM takes unposed RGB views,

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:09.842 line:94%,end align:center
point prompts, and a user-supplied asset library.

00:00:10.442 --> 00:00:13.172 line:94%,end align:center
It retrieves the target assets and estimates

00:00:13.172 --> 00:00:15.583 line:94%,end align:center
their 3D layouts in a single forward pass.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:18.290 line:94%,end align:center
How do we go from a point in an image

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:20.135 line:94%,end align:center
to a 3D object in the room?

00:00:20.475 --> 00:00:23.270 line:94%,end align:center
Take the wooden coffee table in front of the sofa.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:25.780 line:94%,end align:center
A click identifies it in one view.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:28.250 line:94%,end align:center
The other views reveal parts of the table

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:29.818 line:94%,end align:center
that are hard to see from here.

00:00:30.543 --> 00:00:33.403 line:94%,end align:center
The encoder combines appearance features from SAM

00:00:33.403 --> 00:00:36.431 line:94%,end align:center
with geometric features from Depth Anything 3.

00:00:36.771 --> 00:00:38.951 line:94%,end align:center
The prompt carries the camera information

00:00:38.951 --> 00:00:41.315 line:94%,end align:center
and local geometry at the clicked pixel.

00:00:41.655 --> 00:00:44.155 line:94%,end align:center
Attention gathers evidence about the table

00:00:44.155 --> 00:00:46.861 line:94%,end align:center
across views into a set of instance tokens.

00:00:47.585 --> 00:00:50.422 line:94%,end align:center
Now we need to identify the table in the library.

00:00:50.762 --> 00:00:54.902 line:94%,end align:center
DINOv3 encodes canonical views of each candidate.

00:00:54.902 --> 00:00:57.888 line:94%,end align:center
Each reference also carries its viewing direction.

00:00:58.228 --> 00:01:00.648 line:94%,end align:center
The same matcher compares every candidate

00:01:00.648 --> 00:01:02.708 line:94%,end align:center
with the table’s instance tokens.

00:01:02.708 --> 00:01:05.374 line:94%,end align:center
The highest score selects the reference asset.

00:01:06.085 --> 00:01:08.295 line:94%,end align:center
Which way does the selected table face,

00:01:08.295 --> 00:01:09.434 line:94%,end align:center
and where does it belong?

00:01:09.774 --> 00:01:13.064 line:94%,end align:center
The layout decoder reads the same instance tokens,

00:01:13.064 --> 00:01:16.153 line:94%,end align:center
this time alongside the selected asset’s geometry.

00:01:16.493 --> 00:01:19.393 line:94%,end align:center
Three canonical views supply surface positions

00:01:19.393 --> 00:01:20.674 line:94%,end align:center
and viewing directions.

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:23.714 line:94%,end align:center
The decoder predicts translation, rotation,

00:01:23.714 --> 00:01:24.897 line:94%,end align:center
and uniform scale.

00:01:25.543 --> 00:01:28.103 line:94%,end align:center
This transform places the complete table,

00:01:28.103 --> 00:01:29.653 line:94%,end align:center
including its white drawer,

00:01:29.653 --> 00:01:32.050 line:94%,end align:center
in the coordinate frame of the first camera.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.752 line:78%,end align:center
What if the exact table is missing?

00:01:35.352 --> 00:01:38.242 line:78%,end align:center
You can supply our asset library or your own.

00:01:38.242 --> 00:01:41.352 line:78%,end align:center
ALBUM selects the available asset it scores highest

00:01:41.352 --> 00:01:42.883 line:78%,end align:center
and estimates where it fits.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.060 line:78%,end align:center
On ScanNet++, these substitutes can match

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:51.450 line:78%,end align:center
in appearance or in meaning.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:54.409 line:78%,end align:center
Each keeps its original geometry and materials.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.940 line:78%,end align:center
Even surfaces hidden from the cameras are preserved.

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:00.635 line:78%,end align:center
The colored scan gives context for the placement.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:05.320 line:78%,end align:center
Retrieval also preserves the moving parts

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:06.740 line:78%,end align:center
of the source asset.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:08.930 line:78%,end align:center
A drawer can slide or a door can swing

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:10.917 line:78%,end align:center
using its original joint.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:16.420 line:78%,end align:center
Replica supplies its own ground-truth asset libraries.

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:19.701 line:78%,end align:center
Both the rooms and their assets were unseen in training.

00:02:20.301 --> 00:02:22.029 line:78%,end align:center
We use the same network weights.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:26.260 line:78%,end align:center
The retrieved meshes can also be edited.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:28.260 line:78%,end align:center
For this wardrobe, we rigged the front door

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:30.381 line:78%,end align:center
to slide across the other panel.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:37.360 line:97%,end align:center
ALBUM retrieves and places several objects

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:38.757 line:97%,end align:center
in one forward pass.

00:02:39.357 --> 00:02:41.437 line:97%,end align:center
Their point prompts share scene features,

00:02:41.437 --> 00:02:43.773 line:97%,end align:center
and all layouts use the same camera frame.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:47.008 line:94%,end align:center
Where do these library assets come from?

00:02:47.335 --> 00:02:51.555 line:94%,end align:center
ALBUM brings together 6,961 textured assets

00:02:51.555 --> 00:02:53.735 line:94%,end align:center
across 97 indoor categories.

00:02:54.063 --> 00:02:59.113 line:94%,end align:center
Our own collection contributes 2,289 high-quality models

00:02:59.113 --> 00:03:01.167 line:94%,end align:center
created by artists and designers.

00:03:01.494 --> 00:03:05.274 line:94%,end align:center
A further 2,865 come from Artiverse

00:03:05.274 --> 00:03:08.300 line:94%,end align:center
and 1,807 from InternScenes.

00:03:08.627 --> 00:03:11.467 line:94%,end align:center
We checked for duplicates, defective geometry,

00:03:11.467 --> 00:03:12.915 line:94%,end align:center
and implausible dimensions.

00:03:13.242 --> 00:03:17.472 line:94%,end align:center
The library includes 4,236 static assets

00:03:17.472 --> 00:03:21.132 line:94%,end align:center
and 2,725 articulated assets

00:03:21.132 --> 00:03:22.992 line:94%,end align:center
with part and joint metadata.

00:03:23.502 --> 00:03:25.762 line:78%,end align:center
We use these assets to furnish rooms.

00:03:25.762 --> 00:03:27.822 line:78%,end align:center
Support furniture goes in first,

00:03:27.822 --> 00:03:31.246 line:78%,end align:center
then smaller objects are placed on compatible surfaces.

00:03:31.846 --> 00:03:34.636 line:78%,end align:center
Collision and support checks help us construct

00:03:34.636 --> 00:03:37.798 line:78%,end align:center
100,414 furnished layouts.

00:03:38.502 --> 00:03:40.982 line:97%,end align:center
We render multiple views along a camera path

00:03:40.982 --> 00:03:42.320 line:97%,end align:center
through each furnished room.

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:45.920 line:97%,end align:center
Each instance mask links what the camera sees

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:48.620 line:97%,end align:center
to the exact source asset and its 3D layout.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.878 line:97%,end align:center
These links supervise both decoders.

